    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Vatikan',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Vatikan is a Russian Rummy variant using double deck + 2 jokers (106 cards). 2-5 players, 13 each. Key feature: players can REARRANGE existing melds on the table to integrate new cards. First meld must be a sequence from hand. Jokers are wild but can't be moved between melds directly. Draw OR meld each turn (not both).",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Vatikan is described in Andrew Pennycook's A Book of Card Games and is said to be of Central European origin. It belongs to the manipulation rummy family, in which players may rearrange melds on the table; it is very similar to the Italian game Machiavelli and related to Carousel. The tile game Rummikub is a close relative played with tiles rather than cards.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two or more players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '106 cards (2x52 + 2 jokers). A can be high or low.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '13 cards each. Remaining cards form the stock; there is no discard pile.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
